# In-app browser first

Keep users inside onTrack when they open ordinary web content.

## Required

1. Open `https:` links with `@/utils/safe-url` `openHttpsUrl` or `openInAppBrowser` so they appear in an in-app browser first.
2. Let the user explicitly choose any service-provided **Open in App** action from that browser. Do not automatically deep-link or hand an ordinary HTTPS URL to the operating system.
3. Fall back to `Linking.openURL` only when the in-app browser cannot be presented.
4. Continue validating untrusted or synced URLs as HTTPS before opening them.

## Direct handoff exceptions

Direct `Linking.openURL` is allowed when the user explicitly selected an external-app action, or when the target is inherently an OS/app capability such as `tel:`, `sms:`, maps, system settings, an installed-app join link, or an app-store link.

When adding a new external-content journey, regression-test that the first attempt uses the in-app browser and that system handoff is only a fallback or explicit user action.
